      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To implement the `upsert_document.py` file that upserts a JSON document by its primary identifier, I need to choose a concrete external provider. Given the requirement to use a managed NoSQL document store, I will use Amazon DynamoDB as the provider. DynamoDB is a fully managed NoSQL database service that provides fast and predictable performance with seamless scalability. I will use the Boto3 library, which is the Amazon Web Services (AWS) SDK for Python, to interact with DynamoDB. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
